  "answer_core": "Don’t choose a direction yet. Treat the next couple of weeks as a short, low‑cost probe. Two gates determine the real decision: whether the Silva/data path is actually executable, and whether your fallback remains a fully viable, advisor‑supported dissertation route.\n\nStart with your advisor. Before involving anyone else, confirm what support they would offer if you test the Silva path and what resources remain available for the fallback. Then do a focused evidence check with Dr. Silva: what data already exists, who controls access, when you could review it, what collaboration terms look like, and what work would still be yours. Keep this bounded by a clear stop date.\n\nOnly after you have concrete answers on both gates should you commit to a dissertation direction. The right choice is the one that can realistically become a finishable PhD, not the one that feels most exciting.",
